// Package json is the LoGOs twin of the standard encoding/json entry
// points.
//
// It reuses the generated static MarshalJSON and UnmarshalJSON methods
// for .lgo structs with json tags as is: for a type that has generated
// methods the twin calls them. It is the path for what generated methods
// do not cover (any, interface fields, non-string-key maps) and the
// generic entry point over them, plus buffer reuse through MarshalWrite.
// It must not become a second encoder for tagged structs.
//
// Compatibility: output bytes equal encoding/json on the same inputs.
// A struct with generated methods encodes through those methods, which
// are byte-identical to encoding/json by SPEC 10.1. Every other value
// encodes and decodes through encoding/json itself, so equality holds
// by construction. HTML escaping, sorted map keys, cycle errors,
// invalid UTF-8 handling and error texts are those of encoding/json.
//
// Allocation bound: the static struct path calls the generated method
// directly without a per-field reflect walk. The output buffer is the
// single make the generated method performs. Dynamic values (any,
// interface fields, non-string-key maps) allocate exactly as
// encoding/json does. MarshalWrite writes the single marshaled buffer
// once and allocates nothing beyond Marshal.
//
// Diagnostics: malformed input errors carry the encoding/json offset.
// DiagnosticsFor converts an offset to line, column and context only
// when called. Unmarshal never computes line or column, so disabling
// diagnostics costs nothing.
//
// Option rule: an absent option encodes as null (omitted with
// omitempty or omitzero) and a present option encodes as its payload
// alone. Top-level options go through MarshalOption and
// UnmarshalOption in option.lgo, which implement this rule. Struct
// fields of option type go through the generated methods and need the
// upstream static-serializer fix (issue 160, repair commit 11cabf3757);
// until that fix lands they keep the envelope form in both the twin
// and encoding/json.
//
// Failure path: when a MarshalJSON method returns an error, or when its
// output is not valid JSON, the twin delegates the whole value to
// encoding/json and returns that result, so the error value, its type
// field and its text are the original's by construction. The method runs
// a second time inside that call.
package json
